    "conclusion": "The prior analytic-versus-FD discrepancy was caused by the packed nonzero-harmonic branch selecting the real basis response for both real and imaginary controls. After selecting the imaginary response with its packed negative sign, the pointwise gradient error decreases from 1.5e-9 at h to 5.7e-12 at h/4, and the radial/aspect observables are stable to 1e-18/2e-16. The parent cache agrees with the actual parent endpoint to numerical precision; corrected analytic and frozen actual aspect changes differ by only 3.6e-11 fractionally. The analytic oracle is therefore consistent with the independent FD replay for this endpoint, while this diagnostic still makes no trajectory or PDE claim."
